# Local dev config.
#
# Phase 2 (submissions + admin triage) is enabled here AND in .env.production —
# it ships. This file exists because the two builds still differ in one way that
# matters: locally there is no Turnstile site key and no ISA sign-in configured,
# so SuggestButton renders the form anyway (import.meta.env.PROD is false) and
# auth/AuthContext.tsx falls back to its sessionStorage token. That is what lets
# submissions.cy.ts and admin_triage.cy.ts run with no AWS account.
#
# To sign in locally with a real ISA account instead (http://localhost:5173 is a
# registered callback on SlackData's ISA client), copy the three VITE_ISA_*
# lines from .env.production into .env.development.local, and start the API with
# ISA_USER_POOL_ID=eu-central-1_iGaYGKeyJ ISA_CLIENT_ID=2snjdh8i6md0m5n6h9te1hlor1.
#
# Neither difference is a security boundary: the server independently requires a
# captcha whenever it is hosted (utilities/turnstile.py, fails closed) and
# refuses the dev admin token the moment the ISA pool is configured, and always
# when hosted (api/auth.py, deployment.py).
VITE_ENABLE_SUBMISSIONS=true
